{title: 527 - From Every Stormy Wind}
{subtitle: SDA Hymnal #527 • RETREAT • 9.9.8.8}
{lyricist: Hugh Stowell}
{composer: Thomas Hastings}
{key: Bb}
{time: 4/4}
{tempo: Moderato}
{meta: hymn_number 527}
{meta: tune RETREAT}
{meta: meter 9.9.8.8}
{meta: category Christian Life - }

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[F7]From every [Bb]stormy [Eb/Bb]wind [Dm/F]that [Eb]blows,
[Eb/Bb]From [Bb]every [Adim]swelling tide [Bb]of [F/C]woes,
[Bb]There is [Adim]a calm, a [Bb]sure retreat:
[Bb]‘Tis found [Eb/Bb]beneath [Bb]the mercy [F]seat.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[F7]There is a place [Bb]where Jesus sheds The oil [Eb/Bb]of gladness [Dm/F]on [Eb]our heads,
[Bb]A place than all [Eb/Bb]besides [Bb]more sweet; It is the blood-bought [F]mercy seat.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[F7]There is a scene [Bb]where spirits blend, Where friend [Eb/Bb]holds fellowship with friend;
[Bb]Though sundered far, [Eb/Bb]by faith they [Bb]meet Around one common [F]mercy seat.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 4}
[F7]There, there, on angel's [Bb]wings we soar, And earthly [Eb/Bb]cares [Dm/F]molest [Eb]no more,
[Bb]And heaven comes [Eb/Bb]down our souls [Bb]to greet, And glory crowns the [F]mercy seat.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 5}
[F7]Ah! whither should [Bb]we flee for aid, When tempted, [Eb/Bb]desolate dismayed?
[Bb]Or how the hosts [Eb/Bb]of sin defeat, [Bb]Had suffering saints no [F]mercy seat?
{end_of_verse}
